-- data-rename apply: pure attribute change (NAME) on the scratch BOX.
-- Ported from increment_fixture/cases/data_apply.mac; the reference navigates by
-- refno (`={{REF:...}}`), which does NOT work on this db8000 TTY session — see the
-- head note of db8000_zone_members_probe.mac. Navigate by name instead.
--
-- Q REF / Q NAME is emitted twice on purpose: once before the rename and once
-- after. The recorder reads name -> refno from the *apply* log only, so having
-- both names map to the same refno lets the manifest declare the element by
-- either one (it declares the pre-rename name, which reads better).
--
-- restore partner: db8000_scratch_rename_restore.mac (renames it back).

ALPHA LOG "D:/work/plant-code/old/gen-model/scripts/e3d/db8000_scratch_rename_apply.log" OVER
$P CODEX-DB8000-SCRATCH-RENAME-APPLY-ALIVE
/CODEX_DB8000_SCRATCH
Q CE
Q REF
Q NAME
NAME /CODEX_DB8000_SCRATCH_RENAMED
Q CE
Q REF
Q NAME
Q OWNE
SAVEWORK 'CODEX db8000 rename scratch BOX to /CODEX_DB8000_SCRATCH_RENAMED'
$P CODEX-DB8000-SCRATCH-RENAME-APPLY-DONE
ALPHA LOG END
